.TH geectl-meta-set 1  "geectl-meta-set 0.3.0" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-meta\-set \- Set the meta of an OBS project, an OBS package, or a Gitea repository: the description and/or URL, or the whole meta from a file on the OBS arm. The target selects the backend: `\-\-project` (with `\-\-package` for a package) writes OBS meta, `\-\-repo` writes Gitea repo settings. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the write. Field flags change only the given fields; the rest of the meta is kept as it is. `\-\-from\-file` instead replaces the whole meta: fields the file omits are cleared. There is no field flag to clear a field
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl meta set\fR [\fB\-\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-file\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the meta of an OBS project, an OBS package, or a Gitea repository: the description and/or URL, or the whole meta from a file on the OBS arm. The target selects the backend: `\-\-project` (with `\-\-package` for a package) writes OBS meta, `\-\-repo` writes Gitea repo settings. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the write. Field flags change only the given fields; the rest of the meta is kept as it is. `\-\-from\-file` instead replaces the whole meta: fields the file omits are cleared. There is no field flag to clear a field
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The OBS project whose meta to set
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The OBS package in `\-\-project` whose meta to set; the project meta when omitted
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<REPO>\fR
The Gitea repository, as `owner/repo`, whose settings to set
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
A short description
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
A URL with more information; the repository website on the Gitea arm
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-file\fR \fI<FROM_FILE>\fR
Write the given meta file as the whole meta instead of setting fields: the file is the typed JSON `remote project\-meta` / `remote package\-meta` emits (an OBS XML document stays accepted as a legacy format). OBS targets only: Gitea has no whole\-file meta concept. Fields the file omits are cleared. Conflicts with \-\-description and \-\-url
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.3.0
